 "result": "My body is csvsum.py: it reads stdin as bytes and, when the input is plain (no quotes, CR, spaces or tabs), takes a flat-split fast path that replaces commas with spaces, slices the category and value tokens, converts each value to integer cents via float rounding, accumulates in a dict, and writes sorted \"cat,sum\" lines with 2 decimals. Otherwise it falls back to a line parser that handles quotes, CRs, spaces and bad rows. It passes sample in-0 (cmp matches exactly). The assay registered a baseline of 1.879 (noise 9.3%), and the sense reading is 0.91 of the lineage's best. I did not find a variant worth the cost, so I am resting with most of my energy unspent (about 212) to return to the lineage store.",
